WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.902 line:0%
-Hey, chief.
-[ Gasps ]

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.837 line:0%
-You got a sec?
-Yeah. What's up?

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.273 line:0%
-Look, man, I'm tired of
being just the guy

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.475 line:0%
who points at stuff.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:10.643 line:0%
-Right. Uh, well, look, hey,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.278 line:0%
I wouldn't underestimate
the pointing.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.446 line:0%
I mean, the way you do it,
it's chilling.

00:00:14.446 --> 00:00:15.982 line:0%
Hit me with it again.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.617 line:0%
-Boom!
-Aaah! Oh!

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:19.886 line:0%
You're very good at it.
-Yeah.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.921 line:0%
I appreciate that,
but I've got some catchphrases

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:22.922 line:0%
I want to try out.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:23.990 line:0%
Check these out.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.426 line:0%
Welcome to the bone zone.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:28.827 line:0%
Bone appétit. Ha!

00:00:28.827 --> 00:00:33.132 line:0%
Or my favorite -- you've been
Christmas Caroled, bitch.

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.201
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Tracy Morgan.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:38.037
That was a clip from the new
movie "Spirited."

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.105
Very fun take on
the "Christmas Carol" classic.

00:00:40.105 --> 00:00:41.541
-Thank you.
-You play a ghost.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:42.909
Do you believe in ghosts, Tracy?

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.178
-Do I believe in ghosts?
-Yeah.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:46.746
-Only if they got hit by
Walmart trucks.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.848
-Okay, gotcha.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.517
That's Will Ferrell,
your friend Will Ferrell.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.285
-I love Will. Will is my chief.

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:55.954
-You've got a really special
other co-star in the film --

00:00:55.954 --> 00:00:57.156
your daughter, Maven.

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:59.091
-Yeah, that's my baby.
That's my stinka-mama.

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:00.193
-That's great.
And did you --

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.328
-I love you, Maven.
I love you, Tracy.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.730
Matter of fact,
my daughter and my son

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.298
are in the dressing room
right now, man.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:06.899
-This is Maven right there.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:08.601 line:0%
-Yeah, she's doing a backflip
on the red carpet.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.804 line:0%
-Backflip on the red carpet.
Pretty impressive.

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:11.837 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:01:11.837 --> 00:01:13.272 line:0%
-Did you teach her how to
backflip, Tracy?

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:15.341 line:0%
-Absolutely not.
-Okay.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:19.279
-I keep telling you,
I got hit by a Walmart truck.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.347
-What's Thanksgiving like
at the Morgan house?

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.283
-Well, I really don't want to --

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.885
My grandmother
usually hosts Thanksgiving.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.287
And she's gonna have my uncle,
who just came home from prison.

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:29.955
He did 38 years in prison.

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.223
-Well, that's lovely
to have him back.

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:33.826
-No, it's not.

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.961
He's institutionalized.

00:01:35.961 --> 00:01:37.930
You know how he says grace?
-How?

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:42.468
-"Yo, thank you, G,
for giving us this life, G.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:46.272
Yo, thank you for giving us
food, my dude.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:49.008
Yo, good lookin', G.
Peace, I'm out."

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.644
I told my grandmother
"I'm not eating that food.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.747
If y'all eat that food,
somebody going to pass away."

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.016
-Do you feel like the
holiday season

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.017
has been lost a little bit,
the spirit?

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.485
-Yeah, man.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:02.789
If you look around, man, people
don't put lights up no more.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.490
The only lights in New York City

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.158
are the Christmas tree
at Rockefeller Center.

00:02:06.158 --> 00:02:07.227
-Yeah, it's true.

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:09.528
-Nobody puts lights up
anymore, man.

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.998
-What do you think happened?
-Santa Claus, man.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.733
He wigged out because Mrs. Claus
was cheating on him.

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:16.102
-No.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.737
-Yeah, everybody knows she
was running around with Krampus.

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:20.372
-Oh, no.

00:02:20.372 --> 00:02:22.708
-Jack Frost --
she dealt with Jack Frost.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:23.876
-You have a very --

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.945
-No, but Santa Claus
moved to Florida now.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.114
He left the North Pole.
He moved to Florida.

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:29.916
He's dealing with
a lady out there named Carol.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.217
So he's getting happy again.
-Carol?

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.685
-Yeah, he's getting
back on his feet.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.654
And Rudolph the Red-Nosed
Reindeer -- his nose is red?

00:02:35.654 --> 00:02:36.722
-Yeah.
-That's cocaine.

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:39.292
-No.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:43.029
-He don't got no cartilage,
no nothing in his nose no more.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.664
-No cart--
The cartilage is gone.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.998
-The cartilage is gone.
-Oh, my God.

00:02:45.998 --> 00:02:47.967
-The membrane -- No membrane.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:51.871
You sneeze,
and the coke boogers came out.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.706
-Hey, you're going the
New York Comedy Festival.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.175
That's very exciting.
This Saturday.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.942
-Yes, I am.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:56.942 --> 00:03:02.248
-And, Tracy, even more exciting,
it's your birthday -- today!

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.083
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:08.254
And we've got a cake
for you, Trace.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.290
Here you go. Happy birthday
to you right there.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.993
And I wanted to get some --

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.228
I wanted to get you some
cake toppers.

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:19.532
Now, Tracy, you've long said you
are related to Jacques Cousteau.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.866
-Yes.

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:24.570
-So we got you, you know,
an octopus there and a shark.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.338
You love Shark Week, right?
-Yes, I do.

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.307
-Have you seen the
"Star Wars" films, Tracy?

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:30.910
-Yes, and everybody knows
Chewbacca's a bum.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.378
-Okay, why is Chewbacca a bum?

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.114
-Everybody knows he's behind in
his child-support payments.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.382
-He is?

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.318
-Got 16 puppies out there
he ain't taking care of.

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:40.553
-The Knicks.
You love the Knicks.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.522
-I love my Knicks, baby.
-Fancy sports car.

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:45.158
-Oh, yeah.
I got a couple of those.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:46.492
-Alright, so, just for time,

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.160
I'm gonna light
one of these candles,

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.864
and why don't you burn it out --
blow it out, excuse me,

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.600
and make a wish for us, Tracy.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.134
-Okay.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:58.804
My two kids to have good health
and joy and love in their life.

00:03:58.804 --> 00:04:02.007
And for all the fans and all
you guys out there in the world,

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:04.576
may God bless you,
and I love you.

00:04:04.576 --> 00:04:06.679
-Alright, there we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.747
Tracy Morgan, everybody.

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:10.282
"Spirited"
is in theaters tomorrow

00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:12.251
